<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arcadian Gate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 369 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arcadian Gate is the monumental northern gateway of ancient Messene in the south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, built when the city was founded under Theban protection in 369 BCE. A double gate with a circular inner courtyard, it carried the road towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadia">Arcadia</a> and Megalopolis and formed part of a circuit of stone walls and towers some 9 kilometres long. It is among the best-preserved examples of Greek military architecture of the 4th century BCE.</p></div>
